  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 is implicated in the biological activity of NCI-H128 through a series of interconnected targets. The drug is directly linked to A704, which in turn is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and this compound further targets NCI-H128. Similarly, palmarumycin CP18 is also associated with HPAF-II, a target of a related compound that also targets NCI-H128. Additionally, the drug interacts with P2X purinoceptor 1, which is a target of the same compound that targets NCI-H128. These findings suggest that palmarumycin CP18 exerts its biological effects through a shared pathway involving a structurally related compound that ultimately targets NCI-H128. The evidence supports a mechanism where palmarumycin CP18 influences NCI-H128 via a series of targets, likely through a common biochemical pathway or molecular interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for palmarumycin CP18 to modulate NCI-H128 through a complex network of molecular interactions.",
